# FLARE vs {{ other }} - cohort confusion matrix

**What this is.** Both tools assign a categorical superpop label per
sample via argmax over their per-sample proportion vector. The cohort
table sums the per-cluster (FLARE call, {{ other }} call) counts;
{% if src == "rf" %}
rows are RF calls (including MID, which FLARE has no column for) and
columns are FLARE calls.
{% else %}
rows are FLARE calls and columns are Rye calls (no MID on either side
of this comparison).
{% endif %}
Cells carry the cohort-wide count and the row-normalised recall;
diagonals are agreement.

**How to read this chart.** Bright diagonal + high row-recall = the two
tools agree on that superpop cohort-wide. A bright off-diagonal cell,
**outlined in red**, is a systematic disagreement. Compare row-recall
(right margin: diag / row total) with column-precision (bottom margin:
diag / column total). A label with high recall but low precision means
the column-tool over-calls it relative to the row-tool.

